<title>GERMANY: BUNDESBANK DATA SHOW FALL IN NET RESERVES IN WEEK.</title>
<headline>BUNDESBANK DATA SHOW FALL IN NET RESERVES IN WEEK.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bundesbank data released on Tuesday show net currency reserves fell to about 98.6 billion marks in the week ending August 7 from about 99.5 billion marks ($53.4 billion) in the week ending July 31. The Bundesbank provided the following reserve data:</p>
<p>(in billion marks)</p>
<p> Banking week ended		    Aug 7	   July 31</p>
<p> Gross currency reserves	     114.6	   115.5</p>
<p> Foreign liabilities		   16.0	    16.0</p>
<p>-- Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525 ($ = 1.863 German Marks)</p>
